{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Python 3 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Python 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\ndef solve(n, mod):\n    if n <= 3:\n        return 0\n    last = 17\n    ans = 17\n    size = (n-1)*(n-2)//2 + 1\n    flip = 1\n    dp = [[0]*(size+1) for _ in range(2)]\n    dp[0][:4] = [1,2,2,1]\n    for m in range(4, n):\n        sz = m*(m-1)//2\n        ans = (m+1) * last\n        acc = 0\n        cur = dp[flip]\n        prev = dp[1-flip]\n        for i in range(m):\n            acc += prev[i]\n            cur[i] = acc % mod\n        for i in range(m, sz//2+1):\n            acc += prev[i] - prev[i-m]\n            cur[i] = acc % mod\n        for i in range(sz//2+1):\n            cur[sz-i] = cur[i]\n        summ = 0\n        for i in range(sz-1):\n            tmp = 0\n            lo = max(1, -sz+i+m+2)\n            for j in range(lo, m+1):\n                tmp += j * cur[m+2-j+i]\n            summ = (summ + cur[i]) % mod\n            tmp = (tmp * summ) % mod\n            ans = (ans + tmp) % mod\n        last = ans\n        flip ^= 1\n    return ans % mod\n\ndef main():\n    n, mod = map(int, input().split())\n    print(solve(n, mod))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\nusing namespace std;\n\nlong long solve(int n, int mod) {\n    if (n <= 3) return 0;\n    long long last = 17;\n    long long ans = 17;\n    int size = (n-1)*(n-2)/2 + 1;\n    int flip = 1;\n    vector<vector<long long>> dp(2, vector<long long>(size+1, 0));\n    dp[0][0] = 1;\n    dp[0][1] = 2;\n    dp[0][2] = 2;\n    dp[0][3] = 1;\n    for (int m = 4; m < n; ++m) {\n        int sz = m*(m-1)/2;\n        ans = ((m+1) * last) % mod;\n        long long acc = 0;\n        vector<long long>& cur = dp[flip];\n        vector<long long>& prev = dp[1-flip];\n        for (int i = 0; i < m; ++i) {\n            acc = (acc + prev[i]) % mod;\n            cur[i] = acc;\n        }\n        for (int i = m; i <= sz/2; ++i) {\n            acc = (acc + prev[i] - prev[i-m]) % mod;\n            if (acc < 0) acc += mod;\n            cur[i] = acc;\n        }\n        for (int i = 0; i <= sz/2; ++i) {\n            cur[sz - i] = cur[i];\n        }\n        long long summ = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; i < sz-1; ++i) {\n            long long tmp = 0;\n            int lo = max(1, -sz + i + m + 2);\n            for (int j = lo; j <= m; ++j) {\n                tmp += j * cur[m + 2 - j + i];\n            }\n            summ = (summ + cur[i]) % mod;\n            tmp = (tmp % mod) * summ % mod;\n            ans = (ans + tmp) % mod;\n        }\n        last = ans;\n        flip ^= 1;\n    }\n    return ans % mod;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n, mod;\n    cin >> n >> mod;\n    cout << solve(n, mod) << endl;\n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-4.625213477993384e-05, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.0007295330869965255, -0.00038354191929101944, -7.867782187531702e-06, -0.014280857518315315, -1.4781842764932662e-05, 0.0, 0.0, -1.